kboot_display_handoff: T6041 internal display on the macOS 27.2 firmware

The T6041 (M4 Pro) display handoff qualified only the 26.6.2 OS firmware,
so on 27.2 aura logged "no qualified OS firmware for apple,t6041-dcp:
nothing done" and the panel stayed on the boot framebuffer. Every other
check passes on this Mac's 27.2 ADT (mBoot-20457.41.3): addresses, SIDs,
DVA windows, page-table regions, OS log buffers and the firmware segments,
with one more 16K heap segment (region-id-157). Qualify 27.2 as a second
firmware for the J616s/J614s record only, pin its DCP image
(71F140DC-F18D-31B3-9772-537A5CC8400D), and publish firmware-version
<27 2 0> with firmware-compat <27 0 0>: the kernel display driver's
firmware-27 interface. Host tests os-27-2, os-27-2-other-image, os-27-0.
(github:briheet/nixos-m4pro docs/display/dcp-27.2-aura.md)

